  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Republic of Palau Partnership for Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s bilateral aid to the Republic of Palau focuses on the following three strategic objectives:
1.  Reducing the threats from explosive remnants of war.  Palau was a major battlefield in World War II and the vast amounts of unexploded bombs, mines and artillery shells have been a danger to people and a hindrance to effective land use and development.  
2.  Achieving greater gender quality and enhancing women&apos;s empowerment 
3.  Co-finance with the World Bank a project that will reform the Information Communication and Technology (ICT) sector as part of a wider project to lay a new submarine cable that will provide more stable and faster access to the internet for the government, private sector, Non-Government Organisations (NGOs), schools and individuals.  Australian assistance will focus on providing technical assistance to improve the ICT policy and regulatory environment.  Advances in the ICT sector will provide a more enabling environment for the country&apos;s development.</narrative>
  </description>
